    "title": "Firearm Deer Season Resumes On Thursday - NewsBreak",
    "text": "1 hours ago It's time bundle up, put on the blaze orange, and head back out into the woods. The second part of firearm deer season in Illinois runs this Thursday thru Sunday. Hunting begins a half-hour before sunrise and ends a half-hour after sunset. You must have property permits to hunt during the firearm season and be sure to check in your deer at mandatory check stations at Buffalo Rock State Park and the Bureau County Fairgrounds due to past cases of Chronic Wasting Disease. Read full article\nRead in NewsBreak",
